00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:04.480
This is Timothy Hutton. The people of Tibet are&nbsp;
in trouble. Their very culture is in jeopardy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:12.120
But they still whip up an amazing fish curry. And&nbsp;
since 200 of us bought at group.com, we're each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:19.040
getting $30 worth of Tibetan food for just $15 at&nbsp;
Himalayan Restaurant in Chicago. Save the money.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:26.560
Unlock great deals in your town. Groupon.com.&nbsp;
Rupon paid roughly $3 million per spot. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:33.120
there's more. Cuba Gooding Jr. on endangered&nbsp;
whales, Elizabeth Hurley on Amazon deforestation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:37.320
and Timothy Hutton filmed at a&nbsp;
Himalayan restaurant in Chicago.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:44.120
The backlash was immediate. NBC's Adrien Mong&nbsp;
reported the ad managed to do the impossible.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:48.720
Unite the Free Tibet movement and Chinese&nbsp;
nationalists in their shared outrage.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:54.440
On China's Sina Waybo, over 28,000 messages&nbsp;
about the ads appeared [music] within minutes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.440 --> 00:07:00.280
But it was worse than just some bad PR. Groupon&nbsp;
had been trying to expand into China through a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:07.080
partnership with Tencent. That was now in serious&nbsp;
doubt. Mason pulled all three ads within 5 days&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:13.040
and said, "We hate that we offended people&nbsp;
and we're very sorry." But were they?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:20.400
Well, unfortunately, there is a [music] pattern.&nbsp;
In the UK, the Advertising Standards Authority&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:26.320
received over 162 complaints within [music] 3&nbsp;
months regarding Groupon's misleading promotions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:31.600
They breached advertising codes 48 times&nbsp;
in the first 11 months of 2011 alone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:36.680
A San Francisco tour operator filed a class&nbsp;
action lawsuit claiming Groupon was baiting users&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:42.360
with tour ads for [music] deals that didn't even&nbsp;
exist. The Federal Trade Commission had received&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:48.160
over 140 complaints over false advertising&nbsp;
and misleading discounts. At the same time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:52.680
state investigators in Connecticut and Illinois&nbsp;
were questioning whether Groupon's expiring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:58.800
vouchers were even [music] legal. All of this was&nbsp;
happening right before the company went public&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:04.640
and [music] investors were watching. Would all&nbsp;
this ruin Groupon's chances? Would they crash&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:12.920
and burn? November 2011, Groupon was priced&nbsp;
at $20 per share, valuation 12.7 billion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:21.160
The stock opened at $28 on day one, market cap&nbsp;
around 16 billion. one of the biggest tech IPOs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:26.800
since Google itself and almost three times&nbsp;
Google's offer. [music] It was a huge success,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:33.840
but they didn't have time to celebrate. Once a&nbsp;
company goes public, everything is on the table.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:38.800
Now that people could look closer, they&nbsp;
